{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774028921,"nonce":"h0QIsM3ZFTitr8dWMc4Iyl+N4Y0=","title":"Per-model concurrency limits for subagent spawning","message":"When orchestrating parallel subagents, there is no facility to enforce per-model concurrency limits. For example, Gemini 3.1 Pro has stricter rate limits than Opus, so critique agents (which use Gemini) should run one at a time while implementation agents (Opus) can run in parallel.\n\nThis will become more actionable once SDK agent management is more established in Mandible (the Console tab can enforce spawn limits). For now, orchestrators must manually sequence model-specific agents.\n\nDesired behavior:\n- Configurable per-model max concurrency in Mandible settings (e.g., gemini-3.1-pro: 1, opus: 4, sonnet: 6)\n- When spawning a subagent, check the current count of active sessions using that model\n- If at limit, queue the spawn and execute when a slot opens\n- Expose queue status in the Console/Sessions UI\n\nThis is NOT part of the current inbox/work-unit bigbuild — it is infrastructure that becomes easier to manage once SDK agent lifecycle is first-class in Mandible.","files":null}]}